 $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}},{\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ and $\\\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ only. The $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}}$ - ${\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - \\\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ composition range selected here was chosen to represent the bulk chemical composition range relevant to AAS-based cements.\\n![0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg](images/0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg)', 'domain_text': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\\\mathrm{{mass}}\\\\% {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition s', 'original_tokens': 539, 'general_tokens': 539, 'domain_tokens': 421, 'text_adapted': True, 'tokenizer_used': 'matbert_tokenizer_for_domain'}"}, 'highlights': {'content': ['Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而<mark>定</mark>。']}, 'adopted': True}, {'id': '1847ad96-2715-43b3-99a6-a0aab9408c98', 'content': 'end-member of the MA-OH-LDH_ss thermodynamic model used in this work (thick black line) $\\left( {\\mathrm{P} = 1\\text{bar}}\\right)$ . The green triangles at ${\\log }_{10}\\left( {\\mathrm{\\;K}}_{\\mathrm{s}}\\right) = - {56.02}\\left( {{25}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}}\\right.$ and $\\left. {1\\mathrm{{bar}}}\\right)$ , represents the solubility product used previously to describe this phase in the cement chemistry literature. Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006\n### 2.3 Occurrence of ${Mg}$ , Fe and S-bearing phases\nThermodynamic modelling of AAS cements requires consideration of additional constituent elements outside the $\\mathrm{{CaO}} - {\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}\\mathrm{O} - {\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - {\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} - {\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{O}$ system, most notably $\\mathrm{{Mg}}$ , $\\mathrm{{Fe}}$ and $\\mathrm{S}$ , as well as carbonates. While the precipitation of $\\mathrm{{Mg}}$ in AAS cement is generally well explained by its incorporation into Mg-Al LDH phases (Ben Haha et al., 2011b) Richardson et al., 1994; Wang and Scrivener, 1995), 注 2:分期施工的坝应按相应的荷载组合分期进行计算。 there is less consensus regarding the precipitation of Fe and S. Fe was excluded from this work, consistent with the passivated state of this element in GBFS (Bernal et al., 2014a), and S released by the slag was represented as ${\\mathrm{S}}^{2 - }$ with its oxidation limited by using a simulated ${\\mathrm{N}}_{2\\left( \\mathrm{\\;g}\\right) }$ atmosphere in the thermodynamic modelling calculations.\n### 2.4 Other solid phases\nThermodynamic data for cement-related solid phases other than C-(N-)A-S-H gel and MA-OH-LDH were taken from the PSI/Nagra 12/07 thermodynamic database