/Nagra 12/07 thermodynamic database (Thoenen et al., 2013) and the CEMDATA07 thermodynamic database, which was updated to include recently published data for', 'title': '', 'score': 0.05, 'source_type': 'document', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'extra': None, 'headings': [], 'strategy': 'semantic', 'page_number': [1], 'dual_vector_metadata': "{'general_text': 'end-member of the MA-OH-LDH_ss thermodynamic model used in this work (thick black line) $\\\\left( {\\\\mathrm{P} = 1\\\\text{bar}}\\\\right)$ . The green triangles at ${\\\\log }_{10}\\\\left( {\\\\mathrm{\\\\;K}}_{\\\\mathrm{s}}\\\\right) = - {56.02}\\\\left( {{25}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}}\\\\right.$ and $\\\\left. {1\\\\mathrm{{bar}}}\\\\right)$ , represents the solubility product used previously to describe this phase in the cement chemistry literature. Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006\\n### 2.3 Occurrence of ${Mg}$ , Fe and S-bearing phases\\nThermodynamic modelling of AAS cements requires consideration of additional constituent elements outside the $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}} - {\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{O} - {\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} - {\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{O}$ system, most notably $\\\\mathrm{{Mg}}$ , $\\\\mathrm{{Fe}}$ and $\\\\mathrm{S}$ , as well as carbonates. While the precipitation of $\\\\mathrm{{Mg}}$ in AAS cement is generally well explained by its incorporation into Mg-Al LDH phases (Ben Haha et al., 2011b) Richardson et al., 1994; Wang and Scrivener, 1995), 注 2:分期施工的坝应按相应的荷载组合分期进行计算。 there is less consensus regarding the precipitation of Fe and S. Fe was excluded from this work, consistent with the passivated state of this element in GBFS (Bernal et al., 2014a), and S released by the slag was represented as ${\\\\mathrm{S}}^{2 - }$ with its oxidation limited by using a simulated ${\\\\mathrm{N}}_{2\\\\left( \\\\mathrm{\\\\;g}\\\\right) }$ atmosphere in the thermodynamic modelling calculations.\\n### 2.4 Other solid phases\\nThermodynamic data for cement-related solid phases other than C-(N-)A-S-H gel and MA-OH-LDH were taken from the PSI/Nagra 12/07 thermodynamic database (Thoenen et al., 2013) and the CEMDATA07 thermodynamic database, which was updated to include recently published data for', 'domain_text': 'end-member of the MA-OH-LDH_ss thermodynamic model used in this work (thick black line) $\\\\left( {\\\\mathrm{P} = 1\\\\text{bar}}\\\\right)$ . The green triangles at ${\\\\log }_{10}\\\\left( {\\\\mathrm{\\\\;K}}_{\\\\mathrm{s}}\\\\right) = - {56.02}\\\\left( {{25}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}}\\\\right.$ and $\\\\left. {1\\\\mathrm{{bar}}}\\\\right)$ , represents the solubility product used previously to describe this phase in the cement chemistry literature. Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006\\n### 2.3 Occurrence of ${Mg}$ , Fe and S-bearing phases\\nThermodynamic modelling of AAS cements requires consideration of additional constituent elements outside the $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}} - {\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{O} - {\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} - {\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{O}$ system, most notably $\\\\mathrm{{Mg}}$ , $\\\\mathrm{{Fe}}$ and $\\\\mathrm{S}$ , as well as carbonates. While the precipitation of $\\\\mathrm{{Mg}}$ in AAS cement is generally well explained by its incorporation into Mg-Al LDH phases (Ben Haha et al., 2011b) Richardson et al., 1994; Wang and Scrivener, 1995), 注 2:分期施工的坝应按相应的荷载组', 'original_tokens': 597, 'general_tokens': 597, 'domain_tokens': 485, 'text_adap