hrm{S}}^{2 - }$ with its oxidation limited by using a simulated ${\\\\mathrm{N}}_{2\\\\left( \\\\mathrm{\\\\;g}\\\\right) }$ atmosphere in the thermodynamic modelling calculations.\\n### 2.4 Other solid phases\\nThermodynamic data for cement-related solid phases other than C-(N-)A-S-H gel and MA-OH-LDH were taken from the PSI/Nagra 12/07 thermodynamic database (Thoenen et al., 2013) and the CEMDATA07 thermodynamic database, which was updated to include recently published data for', 'domain_text': 'end-member of the MA-OH-LDH_ss thermodynamic model used in this work (thick black line) $\\\\left( {\\\\mathrm{P} = 1\\\\text{bar}}\\\\right)$ . The green triangles at ${\\\\log }_{10}\\\\left( {\\\\mathrm{\\\\;K}}_{\\\\mathrm{s}}\\\\right) = - {56.02}\\\\left( {{25}^{ \\\\circ }\\\\mathrm{C}}\\\\right.$ and $\\\\left. {1\\\\mathrm{{bar}}}\\\\right)$ , represents the solubility product used previously to describe this phase in the cement chemistry literature. Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006\\n### 2.3 Occurrence of ${Mg}$ , Fe and S-bearing phases\\nThermodynamic modelling of AAS cements requires consideration of additional constituent elements outside the $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}} - {\\\\mathrm{{Na}}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{O} - {\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} - {\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{O}$ system, most notably $\\\\mathrm{{Mg}}$ , $\\\\mathrm{{Fe}}$ and $\\\\mathrm{S}$ , as well as carbonates. While the precipitation of $\\\\mathrm{{Mg}}$ in AAS cement is generally well explained by its incorporation into Mg-Al LDH phases (Ben Haha et al., 2011b) Richardson et al., 1994; Wang and Scrivener, 1995), 注 2:分期施工的坝应按相应的荷载组', 'original_tokens': 597, 'general_tokens': 597, 'domain_tokens': 485, 'text_adapted': True, 'tokenizer_used': 'matb