2025-08-04 14:01:57 | INFO     | api.endpoints.qa:generate_sse:415 - [EVENT_DEBUG] 收到事件: <class 'dict'> - {'type': 'knowledge_sources', 'data': {'knowledge_sources': [{'id': 'ec69a6a8-2790-4295-9bc2-157477bac1f1', 'content': '问题: 影响地聚合物混凝土抗压强度的主要因素有哪些？\n答案: A：地聚合物混凝土的抗压强度受多种因素显著影响，包括碱活化剂溶液的类型和浓度、源材料中的钙含量、氢氧化钠的浓度、硅铝比（Si/Al）、养护条件（温度和龄期）以及各种添加剂的种类和掺量。这些因素共同决定了地聚合物化反应的程度和最终形成的聚合网络结构的密实度。', 'title': 'QA: 影响地聚合物混凝土抗压强度的主要因素有哪些？...', 'score': 1.0, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '86c96933-c794-48e3-a661-9f0ebba706ec', 'content': '问题: 对于地聚合物的抗压强度，固化温度、固化期和碱浓度这三个因素中，哪一个被认为是主导因素？其依据是什么？\n答案: A：固化温度被认为是影响地聚合物抗压强度的最主要因素。实验结果表明，无论碱浓度和固化期如何，地聚合物的抗压强度对固化温度的升高（从20°C到60°C）表现出最显著的响应，例如10M NaOH、3天固化期时，强度从20°C的约3 MPa大幅提升至60°C的31.88 MPa。在较高固化温度（如60°C和80°C）下，即使使用较低的碱浓度或较短的固化期，也能获得较高的抗压强度（约30 MPa），这说明高温能更有效地促进地聚合物化反应，导致离子活性增强和致密结构形成，其影响远超碱浓度和固化期。', 'title': 'QA: 对于地聚合物的抗压强度，固化温度、固化期和碱浓度这三个因素中，哪一个被认为是主导因素？其依据是什么？...', 'score': 0.8693566799999999, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '60b5f770-aa34-46a3-9219-552a12cf6713', 'content': '问题: 影响地聚合物高抗压强度的主要因素有哪些？\n答案: A：影响地聚合物高抗压强度的主要因素包括：硬化浆体中未发现膨胀现象；浆体具有良好的工作性能；以及地聚合物浆体在新鲜和硬化状态下均表现出良好的均质性。这些因素共同促进了致密、稳定的微观结构形成，从而提高了宏观抗压强度。', 'title': 'QA: 影响地聚合物高抗压强度的主要因素有哪些？...', 'score': 0.8494592000000001, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'qa_elasticsearch', 'metadata': {}, 'question': '影响地聚合物高抗压强度的主要因素有哪些？', 'answer': 'A：影响地聚合物高抗压强度的主要因素包括：硬化浆体中未发现膨胀现象；浆体具有良好的工作性能；以及地聚合物浆体在新鲜和硬化状态下均表现出良好的均质性。这些因素共同促进了致密、稳定的微观结构形成，从而提高了宏观抗压强度。', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '6726153f-3174-4e1c-b740-b0747a93cd3d', 'content': '问题: 地聚物材料的抗压强度随着其所含骨料体积比的增加而呈现出何种趋势？这种趋势的成因是什么？\n答案: A：地聚物材料的抗压强度随着其所含骨料体积比（1减去GPV）的增加呈现出普遍上升的趋势。这是因为骨料作为强度高、刚度大的组分，能够提供内部骨架支撑，承受大部分外部荷载。随着骨料体积比的增加，浆体在整个材料中的相对体积减少，从而降低了由浆体收缩引起的整体变形和应力。同时，骨料的填充效应有助于形成更致密的结构，减少材料的孔隙率，进而提高材料的整体抗压强度。', 'title': 'QA: 地聚物材料的抗压强度随着其所含骨料体积比的增加而呈现出何种趋势？这种趋势的成因是什么？...', 'score': 0.8445271000000001, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'qa_elasticsearch', 'metadata': {}, 'question': '地聚物材料的抗压强度随着其所含骨料体积比的增加而呈现出何种趋势？这种趋势的成因是什么？', 'answer': 'A：地聚物材料的抗压强度随着其所含骨料体积比（1减去GPV）的增加呈现出普遍上升的趋势。这是因为骨料作为强度高、刚度大的组分，能够提供内部骨架支撑，承受大部分外部荷载。随着骨料体积比的增加，浆体在整个材料中的相对体积减少，从而降低了由浆体收缩引起的整体变形和应力。同时，骨料的填充效应有助于形成更致密的结构，减少材料的孔隙率，进而提高材料的整体抗压强度。', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '9cfb5aac-1625-4628-822c-ac5575f3342f', 'content': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\mathrm{{mass}}\\% {\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition specified in terms of $\\mathrm{{CaO}},{\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ and $\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ only. The $\\mathrm{{CaO}}$ - ${\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - \\mathrm{{MgO}}$ composition range selected here was chosen to represent the bulk chemical composition range relevant to AAS-based cements.\n![0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg](images/0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg)', 'title': '', 'score': 0.05, 'source_type': 'document', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'extra': None, 'headings': [], 'strategy': 'semantic', 'page_number': [1], 'dual_vector_metadata': "{'general_text': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\\\mathrm{{mass}}\\\\% {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition specified in terms of $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}},{\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ and $\\\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ only. The $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}}$ - ${\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - \\\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ composition range selected here was chosen to represent the bulk chemical composition range relevant to AAS-based cements.\\n![0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg](images/0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg)', 'domain_text': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\\\mathrm{{mass}}\\\\% {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition s', 'original_tokens': 539, 'general_tokens': 539, 'domain_tokens': 421, 'text_adapted': True, 'tokenizer_used': 'matbert_tokenizer_for_domain'}"}, 'highlights': {'content': ['Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土<mark>压</mark>力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。']}, 'adopted': True}], 'knowledge_stats': {'total_sources': 5, 'source_types': {'qa_dataset': 4, 'document': 1}, 'average_score': 0.722668596, 'search_time': 0.0}, 'agent_nam