2025-08-04 15:09:59 | INFO     | api.endpoints.qa:generate_sse:458 - [KNOWLEDGE_DEBUG] 收集到的具体知识来源: [{'id': '96a4ceca-fe8d-4b69-87cf-e993ed28836e', 'content': '问题: 地聚合物（Geopolymers）作为一类无机聚合物，其基本结构和形成机制是什么？\n答案: A：地聚合物具有非晶态结构，主要由四面体硅酸盐（(SiO₄)⁴⁻）和铝酸盐（(AlO₄)⁵⁻）单元通过共用所有角原子连接而成。聚合物结构中硅原子被铝原子取代会导致净负电荷，并由碱性阳离子进行补偿。地聚合物化过程是一个复杂的反应，包括固态反应物的溶解、溶解物种的水解以及地聚合物本身的缩聚。起始阶段，氢氧根离子作用于铝硅酸盐前驱体，促使其溶解，释放出单体硅酸盐和铝酸盐物种，随后这些物种通过氧桥形成二维或三维网络结构，并在此过程中脱去水分子，同时保留碱性阳离子。', 'title': 'QA: 地聚合物（Geopolymers）作为一类无机聚合物，其基本结构和形成机制是什么？...', 'score': 1.0, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '142d4f09-cfd3-4e29-9f50-4607f4ecdc57', 'content': '问题: 地聚合物（geopolymer）材料是如何形成的，其基本化学反应机制是什么？\n答案: A：地聚合物是通过将富含铝硅酸盐的原材料（如粒化高炉矿渣GBFS）与水性碱溶液混合，在地球合成或地球化学过程中形成的无定形聚合物。其基本机制涉及碱性溶液对铝硅酸盐原料的溶解，释放出Al和Si离子，随后这些离子在溶液中聚合、缩合，形成具有胶凝性能的三维网络结构。', 'title': 'QA: 地聚合物（geopolymer）材料是如何形成的，其基本化学反应机制是什么？...', 'score': 1.0, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'qa_dataset'}, 'highlights': None, 'question': '', 'answer': '', 'adopted': True}, {'id': 'ea4bf4af-a10d-497e-bb43-5992dda98f9f', 'content': '问题: 地聚物化反应的基本原理是什么？它是如何形成稳定材料的？\n答案: A：地聚物化是一种无机聚合过程，通过碱性活化铝硅酸盐材料实现。在高浓度的碱性氢氧化物或硅酸盐溶液中，铝硅酸盐会发生溶解、缩聚和重排反应，形成具有无定形或半结晶聚合物结构的稳定材料。这些结构以相互连接的Si-O-Al-O-Si键为特征，构成了地聚物体系的胶凝基质。', 'title': 'QA: 地聚物化反应的基本原理是什么？它是如何形成稳定材料的？...', 'score': 0.8152052000000001, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'qa_elasticsearch', 'metadata': {}, 'question': '地聚物化反应的基本原理是什么？它是如何形成稳定材料的？', 'answer': 'A：地聚物化是一种无机聚合过程，通过碱性活化铝硅酸盐材料实现。在高浓度的碱性氢氧化物或硅酸盐溶液中，铝硅酸盐会发生溶解、缩聚和重排反应，形成具有无定形或半结晶聚合物结构的稳定材料。这些结构以相互连接的Si-O-Al-O-Si键为特征，构成了地聚物体系的胶凝基质。', 'adopted': True}, {'id': 'dce250cd-faf5-4430-a0e8-3b158136ea1c', 'content': '问题: 地聚物材料在化学上是如何构成以及其形成机制是什么？这些构成元素如何平衡电荷？\n答案: A：地聚物在化学上由AlO4-和SiO4四面体的交联单元组成，形成无定形铝硅酸盐材料。这些四面体通过共享氧原子形成三维网络结构。为了平衡AlO4-单元中的负电荷，碱金属阳离子（如Li+、Na+、K+和Cs+）充当电荷平衡离子。地聚物的形成过程涉及铝硅酸盐矿物（如偏高岭土或粉煤灰）与高腐蚀性碱性水溶液（MOH，其中M为碱金属阳离子）的反应，从而在环境温度下水热硬化。', 'title': 'QA: 地聚物材料在化学上是如何构成以及其形成机制是什么？这些构成元素如何平衡电荷？...', 'score': 0.8144779, 'source_type': 'qa_dataset', 'source': 'qa_elasticsearch', 'metadata': {}, 'question': '地聚物材料在化学上是如何构成以及其形成机制是什么？这些构成元素如何平衡电荷？', 'answer': 'A：地聚物在化学上由AlO4-和SiO4四面体的交联单元组成，形成无定形铝硅酸盐材料。这些四面体通过共享氧原子形成三维网络结构。为了平衡AlO4-单元中的负电荷，碱金属阳离子（如Li+、Na+、K+和Cs+）充当电荷平衡离子。地聚物的形成过程涉及铝硅酸盐矿物（如偏高岭土或粉煤灰）与高腐蚀性碱性水溶液（MOH，其中M为碱金属阳离子）的反应，从而在环境温度下水热硬化。', 'adopted': True}, {'id': '9cfb5aac-1625-4628-822c-ac5575f3342f', 'content': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\mathrm{{mass}}\\% {\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition specified in terms of $\\mathrm{{CaO}},{\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ and $\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ only. The $\\mathrm{{CaO}}$ - ${\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - \\mathrm{{MgO}}$ composition range selected here was chosen to represent the bulk chemical composition range relevant to AAS-based cements.\n![0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg](images/0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg)', 'title': '', 'score': 0.05, 'source_type': 'document', 'source': 'intelligent_retrieval', 'metadata': {'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'extra': None, 'headings': [], 'strategy': 'semantic', 'page_number': [1], 'dual_vector_metadata': "{'general_text': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\\\mathrm{{mass}}\\\\% {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition specified in terms of $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}},{\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ and $\\\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ only. The $\\\\mathrm{{CaO}}$ - ${\\\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\\\mathrm{O}}_{3} - \\\\mathrm{{MgO}}$ composition range selected here was chosen to represent the bulk chemical composition range relevant to AAS-based cements.\\n![0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg](images/0197456d-5913-7800-aa69-8d5449ef40b1_34_189_203_1268_880_0.jpg)', 'domain_text': 'as the reaction proceeds (Bernal et al., 2015) ### 3.4 Phase diagrams for alkali-activated slag-based cements The prediction of several reaction products in the simulated AAS cements is consistent with the bulk chemical composition of the mixes, which generally lie outside the composition envelope of phase-pure C-(N-)A-S-H gel (Figure 8). Preprint of: R.J. Myers, B. Lothenbach, S.A. Bernal, J.L. Provis, Thermodynamic modelling of alkali-activated slag cements, Applied Geochemistry, 61 (2015): 233-247. Final published version available at http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.apgeochem.2015.06.006 Further analysis of AAS cement chemistry is performed by simulating phase diagrams at a fixed slag reaction extent of ${60}\\\\%$ , a constant amount of ${\\\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\\\mathrm{\\\\;S}$ (equivalent in $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content to a slag composition of 2 mass% ${\\\\mathrm{{SO}}}_{3}$ , which is taken as a representative value of $\\\\mathrm{S}$ content in slags studied in the literature Ben Haha et al., 2011a; Bernal et al., 2014b. Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而定。 Richardson et al., 1994; Shi et al., 2006;) and slag compositions of either 30 or ${40}\\\\mathrm{{mass}}\\\\% {\\\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , with the remaining chemical composition s', 'original_tokens': 539, 'general_tokens': 539, 'domain_tokens': 421, 'text_adapted': True, 'tokenizer_used': 'matbert_tokenizer_for_domain'}"}, 'highlights': {'content': ['Gruskovnjak et al., 2006, Puertas et al., 2011; 注 6:土压力根据坝体外是否填有土石而<mark>定</mark>。']}, 'adopted': True}]
